Description: Link protoc-gen-js against pre-built locale stub library
 protoc-gen-js requires locale symbols from libc++ for iostream initialization.
 The bundled libc++'s locale.cpp cannot be compiled on Debian due to type
 conflicts with glibc headers.
 .
 This patch links protoc-gen-js against a pre-built static library
 (liblocale_stub.a) that contains the necessary locale symbols. The library
 is compiled separately in debian/rules BEFORE the Chromium build starts,
 ensuring it is NOT processed by ThinLTO.
 .
 Previous approaches (Builds 165-174):
 - Adding stub to sources: FAILED (ThinLTO stripped symbols)
 - Removing configs: FAILED (wrong config, -flto=thin remained)
 - Adding -fno-lto flags: FAILED (overridden by global config)
 - Using --undefined: FAILED (stub file missing)
 .
 Pre-built library approach:
 - Compiled outside Chromium build (no GN, no LTO)
 - Symbols preserved in .a file
 - Linked as external library (not processed by ThinLTO)
 - Success probability: 80%
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-11-14

diff --git a/third_party/protobuf-javascript/BUILD.gn b/third_party/protobuf-javascript/BUILD.gn
index d6fa1d7..f4b3332 100644
--- a/third_party/protobuf-javascript/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/protobuf-javascript/BUILD.gn
@@ -12,6 +12,13 @@ if (current_toolchain == host_toolchain) {
       "src/generator/well_known_types_embed.cc",
       "src/generator/well_known_types_embed.h",
     ]
+
+    # Debian: Link against pre-built locale stub library
+    # Library compiled in debian/rules before GN runs
+    # Located at out/Debug_GN_x64/obj/debian/liblocale_stub.a
+    libs = [ "locale_stub" ]
+    lib_dirs = [ "obj/debian" ]
+
     include_dirs = [ "src" ]
     deps = [
       "//third_party/protobuf:protoc_lib",
